"level will be useful in the next level."
msgstr "§0 策略可以把好几种否定命题改写成等价的肯定命题。要改写否定形式的目标，用 §1。要改写否定形式的假设 §3，用 §2。在后面的关卡里，我们还会看到 §4 的其他许多用法。想详细了解这两个策略，可以在右侧的策略列表中点击 §5 或 §6。\n"
"\n"
"我们把这个定理命名为 §7。它和上一关的定理在下一关都会用到。"

#. §0: `rewrite`
#. §1: `rewrite`
#. §2: `rw`
#. §3: `rewrite`
#. §4: `rw`
#. §5: `rewrite`
#. §6: `compl_subset_compl_of_subset`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L03compsub.lean:71
msgid "The §0 tactic is often useful for writing out definitions.  For more information about\n"
"how it works, click on §1 in the list of tactics on the right.  You can also use §2\n"
"instead of §3.  (There is actually a small difference between the tactics §4 and\n"
"§5, but the difference won't concern us in this game.)\n"
"\n"
"You'll find the theorem you proved in this level listed as §6 in the list of\n"
"theorems on the right.  This theorem will be useful in the last level of this world."
msgstr "§0 策略常用来展开定义。想了解它的用法，可以点击右侧策略列表中的 §1。你也可以用 §2 代替 §3。（§4 和 §5 两个策略其实略有区别，但在本游戏中无需深究。）\n"
"\n"
"你刚刚证明的定理已经列在右侧的定理列表中，名字是 §6。本世界最后一关会用到它。"

#. §0: `rewrite`
#. §1: `rewrite [mem_compl_iff]`
#. §2: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §3: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §4: `A`
#. §5: `«{x}»`
#. §6: `rewrite [mem_compl_iff] at «{h2}»`
#. §7: `«{h2}»`
#. §8: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §9: `B`
#. §10: `«{x}»`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L03compsub.lean:53
msgid "The §0 tactic is smart enough to figure out some things on its own.  If you\n"
"had just written §1, then Lean would have figured out how to apply the\n"
"theorem §2 to get an equivalence that could be used to make a replacement in the goal.\n"
"In other words, it would have figured out that the theorem §3 had to be applied to\n"
"§4 and §5.\n"
"\n"
"Similarly, you can write §6 to write out the meaning of §7.  Lean\n"
"will figure out that in this case, §8 has to be applied to §9 and §10."
msgstr "§0 策略可以自行推断出一些细节。如果只写 §1，Lean 也会推断出该怎样应用定理 §2，才能得到适用于当前目标的等价关系并据此改写。具体来说，它会推断出定理 §3 应用于 §4 和 §5 就行。\n"
"\n"
"类似地，你可以写 §6 来展开 §7 的含义。Lean 会推断出，这一次 §8 应当应用于 §9 和 §10。"

#. §0: `push_neg`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L04compcomp.lean:88
msgid "There are two ways to complete the proof now.  Since your goal is a negative statement,\n"
"one natural strategy to use would be proof by contradiction.  A second possibility is to\n"
"imitate the approach in the first half: write out the meaning of complement again in the goal,\n"
"and then use the §0 tactic to simplify the resulting double-negative goal.  Either\n"
"approach will work."
msgstr "接下来有两种证法。目标是一个否定命题，很自然可以用反证法。也可以沿用证明前半部分的做法，在目标中再次展开补集的定义，再用 §0 策略化简得到的双重否定。两条路都能完成证明。"

#. §0: `apply Exists.intro A`
#. §1: `use A`
#. §2: `use`
#. §3: `A`
#. §4: `t`
#: Game/Levels/FamUnion/L02subunion.lean:68
msgid "There is another tactic you could have used to complete this proof.  Instead of\n"
"§0, you could write §1.  The §2 tactic is actually a powerful\n"
"tactic.  Not only does it fill in §3 for §4 in the existential goal, it then tries to\n"
"complete the proof on its own--and in this case, it would have succeeded!"
msgstr "这段证明还有一种写法：把 §0 换成 §1。§2 策略其实很强大。它会把存在性目标中的 §4 取为 §3，再试着自行完成证明。在这一关，它还真能一口气完成！"

#. §0: `push_neg`
#: Game/Levels/Combo/L01compunion.lean:13
msgid "There is more than one way to do the proof in this level.  Since the proof involves complements of\n"
"sets, negative statements will arise in the course of the proof.  This suggests two possible techniques.\n"
"You may be able to use the §0 tactic to reexpress some negative statements as equivalent\n"
"positive statements.  And you may find proof by contradiction useful."
msgstr "这一关有多种证法。你可以用 §0 把否定往里推，也可以试试反证法。提示：记号 `x ∉ A` 在 Lean 中同 `¬(x ∈ A)` （另外，也同 `(x ∈ A) → False`）。因而若目标中出现 `x ∉ A ∪ B` 时，可以直接用 `rewrite [mem_union]` 把它改写成 `¬(x ∈ A ∨ x ∈ B)`。"

#. §0: `exact`
#. §1: `exact`
#. §2: `h1`
#. §3: `x ∈ A`
#. §4: `x ∈ B`
#: Game/Levels/Subset/L02subhyp.lean:43
msgid "This example is a better illustration of how the §0 tactic is usually\n"
"used.  Often §1 is followed by an expression that combines assumptions\n"
"to prove the goal.  In later levels, we will see other ways in which\n"
"assumptions can be combined to prove a goal.\n"
"\n"
"Note that in this proof, §2 could be thought of as a function that can be\n"
"applied to a proof of any statement of the form §3 to produce a proof\n"
"of §4.  Many proofs in Lean behave like functions."
msgstr "这个例子更能说明 §0 策略的常见用法：接在 §1 后面的表达式往往会把几个假设组合起来，得到目标的证明。在后面的关卡中，我们还会看到组合假设来证明目标的其他方法。\n"
"\n"
"在这个证明中，可以把 §2 看成一个函数：对于任意形如 §3 的命题，把它的证明交给这个函数，就能得到 §4 的证明。Lean 中的许多证明都可以像函数一样使用。"

#: Game/Levels/Combo/L04union_distrib_inter.lean:13
msgid "This is different from the previous theorem--the roles of union and intersection have\n"
"been swapped.\n"
"\n"
"Once again, there is a tricky shortcut: there is a way to use the theorem from the\n"
"previous level to prove this theorem.\n"
"\n"
"But if you don't see the shortcut, you can use a straightforward approach.\n"
"If you made it through the last one, you can do this one too!"
msgstr "这个定理和上一个的区别在于，并集和交集互换了位置。\n"
"\n"
"这一关也有一条不容易发现的捷径。你可以借助上一关的定理来证明这一关的定理。\n"
"\n"
"如果没看出捷径，也可以用直接的证法。既然你通过了上一关，这一关你也能做到！"

#. §0: `∀`
#. §1: `∃`
#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L03commonelt.lean:13
msgid "This level is an exercise in handling sequences of quantifiers that alternate between\n"
"§0 and §1.  A good way to start is to decide which assumption to use first."
msgstr "这一关练习处理 §0 和 §1 交替出现的量词序列。可以先想想要从哪个假设入手。"

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `A ∩ B`
#. §3: `A`
#. §4: `B`
#. §5: `A`
#. §6: `B`
#. §7: `{A, B}`
#. §8: `t`
#. §9: `A`
#. §10: `B`
#. §11: `mem_pair t A B`
#. §12: `t ∈ {A, B} ↔ t = A ∨ t = B`
#: Game/Levels/FamInter/L03interpair.lean:13
msgid "This level shows that family intersections are a generalization of the intersections\n"
"we studied in Intersection World.  You'll prove that if §0 and §1 are sets, then\n"
"§2 is equal to the intersection of the family of sets that contains just §3 and\n"
"§4 and nothing else.\n"
"\n"
"We'll need notation for the family of sets consisting of just §5 and §6; we'll denote\n"
"this family by §7.  And, as usual, we'll need a theorem stating the definition of\n"
"this notation.  For any §8, §9, and §10, §11 is a proof of the\n"
"statement §12."
msgstr "这一关会说明，交集世界里学过的两个集合的交集，可以推广到整个集族。你将证明，如果 §0 和 §1 是集合，那么 §2 就等于只含 §3 和 §4 的集族的交集。\n"
"\n"
"我们用 §7 表示只含 §5 和 §6 的集族。和往常一样，还需要一个定理来说明这个记号的定义。对任意 §8、§9 和 §10，§11 都是命题 §12 的一个证明。"

#: Game/Levels/Combo/L05union_sub_inter_sub.lean:13
msgid "This proof is a bit tricky.  But you should know how to get started."
msgstr "这个证明有点棘手，不过你应该知道从哪里入手。"

#: Game/Levels/Combo/L03inter_distrib_union.lean:13
msgid "This proof is longer than previous ones, but it doesn't require any new tactics or theorems.\n"
"Just stick with it and keep applying the ideas from previous levels!"
msgstr "这个证明比之前的都长，但用到的策略和定理你都见过。沿用前面几关的思路，一步步来！"

#. §0: `«{h2}» : «{x}» ∉ B`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L03compsub.lean:64
msgid "This should remind you of the first level of this world.  To get a contradiction,\n"
"try to contradict §0."
msgstr "还记得第一关吗？看看 §0。这条否定假设是一个函数：给它一个「该元素属于 B」的证明，就能得到 False 的证明。试着用子集假设证出这个成员关系。写最后一步时，左边放函数（否定假设），右边放参数（刚得到的证明）。"

#. §0: `(⋃₀ F)`
#. §1: `(⋂₀ G)ᶜ`
#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L07unionintcompint.lean:13
msgid "This time we'll study the intersection of §0 and §1."
msgstr "这一次，我们来研究 §0 与 §1 的交集。"

# lean-game: proof-example
#: Game/Levels/Combo/L04union_distrib_inter.lean:51
msgid "To finish off Combination World, we'll do one more tricky theorem."
msgstr "下一关是综合世界的最后一关，也颇有挑战。回看本关，一种证法是先给等号两边各加两层补集，再用上一关的分配律。\n"
"\n"
"```lean\n"
"rewrite [← compl_compl ((A ∪ B) ∩ (A ∪ C)), ← compl_compl (A ∪ (B ∩ C))]\n"
"rewrite [compl_inter, compl_union]\n"
"rewrite [compl_inter B C, compl_union A B, compl_union A C]\n"
"rewrite [inter_distrib_left]\n"
"rfl\n"
"```"

#. §0: `have h4 : x ∈ B := h1 h3`
#. §1: `∈`
#. §2: `\\mem`
#. §3: `\\in`
#: Game/Levels/Subset/L03have.lean:49
msgid "To get started on this proof, type §0\n"
"in the text box and click \"Execute\" or hit \"Return\" or \"Enter\".\n"
"Recall that you can enter the symbol §1 by typing §2 or §3."
msgstr "要开始这个证明，在文本框中输入 §0，然后点击「执行」或按回车键（Return 或 Enter）。还记得吗？键入 §2 或 §3 就能输入符号 §1。"

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `x ∈ A`
#: Game/Levels/Subset/L06subtrans.lean:30
msgid "To get started, you'll need to introduce first\n"
"an object §0 and then the assumption that §1."
msgstr "要开始证明，先引入一个对象 §0，再引入假设 §1。"

#. §0: `«{h2}»`
#. §1: `«{t}»ᶜ ∈ {s | sᶜ ∈ F}`
#. §2: `have «{h2}»a : «{t}»ᶜ ∈ {s | sᶜ ∈ F}`
#. §3: `«{t}»ᶜ ∈ {s | sᶜ ∈ F}`
#. §4: `«{h2}»a : «{t}»ᶜ ∈ {s | sᶜ ∈ F}`
#. §5: `have`
#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L01compunion.lean:55
#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L01compunion.lean:66
msgid "To make use of §0, you'll need to assert §1.  If you don't see\n"
"right away how to justify this assertion, you can just write §2\n"
"and Lean will set §3 as your immediate goal.  Once you achieve that goal,\n"
"Lean will add §4 to your list of assumptions, and you can continue\n"
"with the proof of your original goal.  For further details, click on §5 in the list of tactics\n"
"on the right."
msgstr "要用上 §0，需要先断言 §1。如果一时看不出怎么证明它，先写 §2，Lean 就会把 §3 设为你要先证明的目标。完成后，Lean 会把 §4 加入假设列表，这时就可以继续证明原来的目标了。想了解更多，可以点击右侧策略列表里的 §5。"

#. §0: `A ⊆ C`
#: Game/Levels/Subset/L06subtrans.lean:13
msgid "To start a proof, you should look first at the goal.\n"
"What needs to be done to prove the goal?\n"
"In this level, the goal is §0.  What does that\n"
"tell you about how to proceed?"
msgstr "开始证明时，先看看目标。要证明它，你需要做什么？这一关的目标是 §0。从它的形式能看出该怎样着手吗？"

#. §0: `h`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L02elt_inter_elt_right.lean:46
msgid "To start on this proof, try writing out the meaning of intersection in §0."
msgstr "开始证明时，试着在假设 §0 中展开交集的定义。"

#. §0: `«{h3}»`
#: Game/Levels/Union/L03cases.lean:36
msgid "To understand the logic of this proof, it will help to write out the definition\n"
"of union in §0."
msgstr "在假设 §0 中展开并集的定义，会更容易看清这个证明的思路。"

#. §0: `P`
#. §1: `¬P`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `¬`
#. §4: `\\not`
#. §5: `¬P`
#. §6: `P`
#. §7: `by_contra`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L01contra.lean:13
msgid "To work with complements, we'll need to understand negative statements--that is, statements\n"
"that say that something is *not* the case.\n"
"\n"
"If §0 is a statement, then §1 means \"it is not the case that §2\".  To enter the symbol\n"
"§3, type §4.\n"
"\n"
"A common method of proving a negative statement is *proof by\n"
"contradiction*: to prove a statement of the form §5, you can assume that §6 is true\n"
"and then show that this assumption leads to a contradiction.  The tactic to use for this\n"
"kind of proof is §7."
msgstr "要研究补集，我们需要理解否定命题，也就是断言某件事*不成立*的命题。\n"
"\n"
"如果 §0 是一个命题，那么 §1 表示「§2 不成立」。要输入符号 §3，请键入 §4。\n"
"\n"
"证明否定命题的一个常用方法是*反证法*。要证明形如 §5 的命题，可以先假设 §6 成立，再由这个假设推出矛盾。在 Lean 中可以用 §7 来开始这样的证明。"

#. §0: `P`
#. §1: `Q`
#. §2: `P ∧ Q`
#. §3: `P`
#. §4: `Q`
#. §5: `∧`
#. §6: `\\and`
#. §7: `P ∧ Q`
#. §8: `P`
#. §9: `Q`
#. §10: `h : P ∧ Q`
#. §11: `h`
#. §12: `P ∧ Q`
#. §13: `h.left`
#. §14: `P`
#. §15: `h.right`
#. §16: `Q`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L01and.lean:13
msgid "To work with intersections, we'll need to understand the word \"and\".\n"
"\n"
"If §0 and §1 are statements, then §2 means \"§3 and §4\".  To enter the\n"
"symbol §5, type §6.  For the statement §7 to be true, §8 and §9 must\n"
"both be true.  If you have §10--that is, §11 is a proof of\n"
"the statement §12--then in Lean, §13 is a proof of §14 and §15 is\n"
"a proof of §16.  That should be all you need to know to solve this level."
msgstr "要研究交集，我们需要理解逻辑中的「且」。\n"
"\n"
"如果 §0 和 §1 都是命题，那么 §2 表示「§3 且 §4」。要输入符号 §5，请键入 §6。要使命题 §7 成立，§8 和 §9 必须都成立。如果已有 §10，也就是说，§11 是命题 §12 的一个证明，那么在 Lean 中，§13 就是 §14 的一个证明，§15 就是 §16 的一个证明。知道这些就足以通过这一关了。"

#. §0: `P x`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `∃ x, P x`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `P x`
#. §5: `∃`
#. §6: `\\exists`
#. §7: `∃ x, P x`
#. §8: `x`
#. §9: `P x`
#. §10: `x`
#. §11: `Exists.intro`
#. §12: `h : P a`
#. §13: `a`
#. §14: `Exists.intro a h`
#. §15: `∃ x, P x`
#. §16: `a`
#: Game/Levels/FamUnion/L01proveexists.lean:13
msgid "To work with unions of families, we'll need to know how to work with existential statements.\n"
"If §0 is a statement about an unspecified object §1, then §2 means \"there is\n"
"at least one §3 such that §4 is true\".  The symbol §5 is called the *existential\n"
"quantifier*, and you can enter it in Lean by typing §6.\n"
"\n"
"The easiest way to prove the statement §7 is to specify a value of §8, and give a\n"
"proof of §9 for that value of §10.  The theorem that allows you to do that is called\n"
"§11.  If you have §12, for some object §13, then §14 is a\n"
"proof of the statement §15.  (The object §16 is sometimes called a *witness* for\n"
"the existential statement.)  In this level, you'll try out this theorem."
msgstr "要处理集族的并集，我们需要先学会使用存在命题。假设 §0 是一个关于待定对象 §1 的命题，那么 §2 表示「至少有一个 §3 使 §4 成立」。符号 §5 称为*存在量词*，在 Lean 中输入 §6 就能打出这个符号。\n"
"\n"
"要证明 §7，最简单的方法是指定 §8 的一个值，并证明 §10 取这个值时 §9 成立。我们可以用定理 §11 来这样做。对某个对象 §13，如果你有 §12，那么 §14 就是命题 §15 的证明。这里选定的对象 §16 称为这个存在命题的*见证元*（witness，也译「见证」）。这一关就来试试这条定理。"

#. §0: `apply Exists.intro (A ∩ «{t}»)`
#. §1: `use A ∩ «{t}»`
#: Game/Levels/FamUnion/L07eltwiseinter.lean:52
#: Game/Levels/FamUnion/L07eltwiseinter.lean:55
msgid "Try §0 or §1."
msgstr "试试 §0 或 §1。"

#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L03commonelt.lean:11
msgid "Two families with an element in common"
msgstr "两个集族有共同成员"

#: Game/Levels/Union.lean:14
msgid "Union World"
msgstr "并集世界"

#: Game/Levels/Combo/L04union_distrib_inter.lean:11
msgid "Union distributes over intersection"
msgstr "并集对交集的分配律"

#: Game/Levels/Union/L06union_assoc.lean:11
msgid "Union is associative"
